:: Temple Chastity Prayer
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<temple_effects>><<effects>>
<<set _chastityPrayerReason to templeChastityRefusalReason()>>
<<pass 180>>
You kneel before the altar and pray for the strength to make yourself worthy of release, whatever that takes.
<br><br>
<<if _chastityPrayerReason is "stats" or _chastityPrayerReason is "reputation" or _chastityPrayerReason is "crime">>
	<<run templeChastityGainTrust(_chastityPrayerReason)>>
	<<if templeChastityTrusted(_chastityPrayerReason)>>
		<span class="blue">Something in your bearing has changed. Whatever <<he>> was looking for, <<he>> won't hold it against you again.</span>
	<<elseif _chastityPrayerReason is "stats">>
		<span class="blue">Something in you settles, just a little. Prayer alone won't fix it, but every visit counts.</span>
	<<elseif _chastityPrayerReason is "reputation">>
		<span class="blue">You feel like you've atoned, just a little. Whether anyone else notices is another matter.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="blue">You pray for the strength to face what you've done. It doesn't erase the warrant, but it settles something in you.</span>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	Nothing changes. Whatever's keeping you locked away isn't something prayer alone can fix.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Temple Chastity]]>><</link>>

:: Temple Chastity Plead
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<temple_effects>><<effects>>
<<set _templePleadReason to templeChastityUnderlyingRefusalReason()>>
<<He>> pauses when you ask <<him>> to reconsider, studying you for a long moment.
<br><br>
<<if _templePleadReason is "crime">>
	<<He>> sighs. "I can't pretend a warrant doesn't exist, but I can't pretend people don't change, either." <<His>> gaze doesn't waver. "Show me you mean it. Do right by someone who needs it, and I'll take that over a warrant."
<<elseif _templePleadReason is "reputation">>
	<<He>> sighs. "I can't unhear what I've heard, but reputations aren't set in stone." <<He>> studies you a moment longer. "Show me you mean it. Do right by someone who needs it, and I'll take that over rumours."
<<else>>
	<<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "That's not something I can bend on. Prayer is the only path I can offer you there."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _templePleadReason is "reputation" or _templePleadReason is "crime">>
	<<set $templeGoodwillUnlocked to $templeGoodwillUnlocked || {}>>
	<<set $templeGoodwillUnlocked[_templePleadReason] to true>>
	<i>Jordan will be watching for a genuine act of kindness, not empty words. The soup kitchen might be a good place to start.</i>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Temple]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Soup Kitchen Goodwill
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<effects>>
<<set $daily.templeGoodwillFed to true>>
<<generatey1>><<person1>>
As you step inside, a small <<person>> tugs at your sleeve. <<Hes>> thin, and <<his>> clothes have seen better days. "Please," <<he>> says, looking up at you. "I haven't eaten today."
<br><br>
<<set _hasDish to Object.keys($foodstuff).some(key => setup.foodstuff[key].category is "dish" and $foodstuff[key].amount gte 1)>>
<<if _hasDish>>
	<i>You could share something you've cooked, if you have it on you. Raw ingredients won't do <<him>> much good.</i>
	<br><br>
	<<food_gift_list>>
	<<link [[Give them a meal|Soup Kitchen Goodwill Give]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Walk past|Soup Kitchen Goodwill Ignore]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You have nothing cooked on you to share. <i>Maybe you should learn to make something, for next time.</i>
	<br><br>
	<<unset $templeGoodwillReason>>
	<<link [[Next|Soup Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Soup Kitchen Goodwill Give
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<effects>>
You hand over <<recipe_name $gift>>. <<Hes>> hesitant at first, then takes it with both hands, eyes wide.
<br><br>
"Thank you," <<he>> says, before hurrying off to eat in a corner.
<br><br>
<<tending_give $gift -1>>
<<run templeChastityGainTrust($templeGoodwillReason)>>
<<if templeChastityTrusted($templeGoodwillReason)>>
	<span class="green">Something about the moment stays with you. Whatever Jordan was holding against you, you don't think <<he>> would anymore, if <<he>> saw this.</span>
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">It's a small thing, but it feels like it matters.</span>
<</if>>
<<unset $templeGoodwillReason>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Soup Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Soup Kitchen Goodwill Ignore
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<effects>>
You look away and step past <<him>>. <<Hes>> doesn't press the point.
<br><br>
<<unset $templeGoodwillReason>>
<<link [[Next|Soup Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Soup Kitchen Charity Donation
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<effects>>
River does not reach for the envelope. "What do you want in return?"
<br><br>
"Nothing," the stranger says. "I saw those children eating as though it might be their only proper meal today. I have more than I need, and they need it. Let me do one good thing."
<br><br>
River studies the stranger in silence. "No names. No photographs," <<he>> says at last. "You don't come back later expecting gratitude from them."
<br><br>
"Agreed."
<br><br>
River accepts the envelope. The stranger leaves without another word. <<He>> counts the money, then divides part of it between several smaller envelopes. The orphans stare as <<he>> hands the envelopes around.
<br><br>
River pushes one toward you. You hesitate. "You're an orphan too," <<he>> says. "Take it."
<br><br>
There's <<income $daily.soupKitchenCharity "orphanageCharity">> inside.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Soup Kitchen]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Soup Kitchen Steal
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<effects>>
<br>
You look through the cabinets. There are many people here, but they're busy. You should still be careful though.<br><br>

<<if Time.weekDay is 1>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "haddock" "lemon">>
<<elseif Time.weekDay is 2>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "salmon" "broccoli">>
<<elseif Time.weekDay is 3>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "trout" "lemon">>
<<elseif Time.weekDay is 4>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "cod" "potato">>
<<elseif Time.weekDay is 5>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "clam" "onion">>
<<elseif Time.weekDay is 6>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "prawn" "garlic_bulb">>
<<else>>
	<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "prawn" "lemon">>
<</if>>

<<kitchenicon "soup">><<link [[Back|Soup Kitchen Kitchen]]>><</link>>

:: temple Kitchen Steal Result
<<effects>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 700>><<skulduggerycheck>>
<br><br>

<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	You look around and quickly reach for <<recipe_name $phase "plural">> before anybody can bear witness to your crimes. <<tending_pick $phase 3 6>>
	You probably shouldn't take more or the <<monks>> will realize.<br><br>
	
	<<kitchenicon "soup">><<link [[Return to the kitchen|Soup Kitchen Kitchen]]>><</link>><br><br>
	<<if Time.weekDay is 1>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "haddock" "lemon">>
	<<elseif Time.weekDay is 2>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "salmon" "broccoli">>
	<<elseif Time.weekDay is 3>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "trout" "lemon">>
	<<elseif Time.weekDay is 4>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "cod" "potato">>
	<<elseif Time.weekDay is 5>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "clam" "onion">>
	<<elseif Time.weekDay is 6>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "prawn" "garlic_bulb">>
	<<else>>
		<<ingredientsSuppliesSteal "vegetable_oil" "salt" "flour" "prawn" "lemon">>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<npc River>><<generatey2>><<person2>><<generatey3>>
	You do your best not to look suspicious while stealing the <<recipe_name $phase "plural">>, but you attract a gaze of another volunteer regardless
	"What are you doing?" <<He>> asks too loudly for your liking. "You shouldn't be stealing from the soup kitchen. It's wrong!"<br>
	"What? Somebody is stealing?" A <<person3>><<person>> joins.<br>
	"It's not okay! If you're hungry, you should just ask for the soup!"<br>
	The commontion attracks an attention of some <<monks>> as well as River, who glares at you in disappointment. Even some of people who came in for the food look at you. You won't get away with it.<br><<lllgrace>><<grace -15>><<npcincr River love -5>><<lllove>><<famegood -15>>
	"You came here to help, not to steal more food," River says. "If you can't help yourself, then leave."<br>
	<<person1>>You leave the kitchen, <<his>> blue eyes following your stept to ensure you won't cause any more problems. You probably shouldn't return for now.<br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Wolf Street]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><<set $weekly.theft.temple.Ban to true>><</link>>
<</if>>
